{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Dressing the Part"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "New Expectations "}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Uses of the Future Perfect and Future Continuous Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous tense</span> to talk about something that <span class=\"underline\">will be in progress</span> at a particular time in the future.  <br>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect tense</span> to talk about something that <span class=\"underline\">will be complete</span> by a certain time in the future. This is the past in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You also use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> to talk about future events that are decided.  <br> For example: <br><span class=\"italic\"> I'll be wearing a grey jacket and tie.</span>  (You have already decided what you will be wearing).  <br><br>When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span>, you often refer to a time period.  <br>For example:  <br><span class=\"italic\">My internship will have lasted over two months (by then)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will have worn that suit two times before. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "My internship will have lasted over two months. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will be wearing a grey jacket and tie I bought."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Our business partners will be staying for two weeks."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals for Request: Could and Would "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\">modals</span> <span class=\"italic\">would</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> make requests more indirect than the <span class=\"strong\">modal </span><span class=\"italic\">can</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use indirect styles of speech and writing in formal situations.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:  <br><span class=\"italic\">Could you please confirm your attendance at your earliest convenience?  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use the structure <span class=\"italic\">We would like to \u2026 </span> to make requests in a formal way.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:  <br><span class=\"italic\">We would like to invite you for an interview on Wednesday, January 22nd.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "These structures are indirect and therefore more polite. It is common to read or hear this type of language in a work setting. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We would like to invite you for an interview on Wednesday, January 22nd."}, {"type": "example", "content": "At that time, we would request that you provide the names of three people who can attest to your professional skills. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We would also like you to elaborate on your volunteer experience at the campus newspaper. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If possible, could you please prepare a portfolio of the work you completed in the past?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Could you please confirm your attendance at your earliest convenience?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "web content editor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person responsible for writing and publishing information for publications on the internet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Thank you for expressing interest in the position of Web Content Editor at our publication Never Odd Or Even."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about an interview."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "educational background"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the programs of study a person has completed in the past"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your resum\u00e9 demonstrates that you have the appropriate educational background."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "qualifications"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the things a person can do because of their education or specialized training"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  You have excellent qualifications for this position. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "committee"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a group of people who work together on a task to reach a common goal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The selection committee will be ready to talk to you at 10:00 a.m."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to elaborate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give more details about something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We would like you to elaborate on your volunteer experience at the campus newspaper."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le13ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, talk about situations in which one person makes formal requests and the other person responds (for example, an interview, a meeting, a presentation, etc.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Select one situation and the requests."}, {"type": "text", "content": "One person writes an e-mail making requests."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The other person writes an e-mail responding to the requests. Make sure you u